# Toy model superposition replication (https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.10652)
This repository is a replication of a result from Anthropic's 2022 paper "Toy Models of Superposition".

The claim I tested: Higher the sparsity of data, superposition occurs more.

## Summary + Polysematic Figure

To test this superposition hypothesis, we trained two small model. The two models were: Linear Model, and a Relu Model.


## Bug Fixes
Bug fix (13 Nov 2026): earlier versions created each model once, outside the seed and sparsity loops, so every run continued training the previous run’s weights instead of starting fresh; each run now trains a newly initialised model, and the figures above come from the corrected version.

